    "body": "Fixes #8756\n\n`timed_op` called `get_accelerator().synchronize()` for every wrapped comm op whenever comms logging was enabled. Ops not selected by `prof_ops`, `prof_all` or `prof` get no timer and no record, so the sync was pure overhead.\n\nThe sync is now guarded by `should_profile`. The MPI `cdb.barrier()` is unchanged.\n\nTest: `test_collective_profiling` now counts `synchronize()` calls. It must be 0 for the `unselected` case and 1 for `prof_all`, `prof`, and both `prof_ops` cases. Without the fix the 8 `unselected` cases fail; with it all 52 tests in `test_comms_logger.py` pass. yapf is clean.\n\nVerified on a node with A40 GPUs, but the tests use a mocked backend and accelerator, so no GPU was exercised. Not verified: real NCCL/MPI runs, training step timing, or the rest of the unit test suite.\n\nThanks to @marcusacosta for the report.\n\nThis change was prepared by an automated AI agent (Claude) and verified as described above.",
